# The vLLM pin: the latest GitHub release, the image repository of each flavor, the row each
# flavor serves by default, which moves with the release rather than on demand, and native vLLM's
# Python. One release serves every flavor: host/vllm.sh names the image <repository>:<release>,
# in the repository of the flavor it resolves (vllm_flavor). cuda's is the release's default tag,
# vLLM's CUDA 13.0 multi-arch build, not a variant such as -ubuntu2404 or -cu129: both pinned
# releases of the update walk (v0.31.0, v0.32.0) publish it for arm64, and so does v0.33.0.
# rocm's is vLLM's official ROCm image of the same release, its default tag. Sourced by
# scripts/currency.sh, which reads only the release, and host/vllm.sh, and through it
# host/vllm-native.sh.
#
# On v0.33.0, rocm's default tag is its ROCm 10.0 build, the same image as v0.33.0-rocm100
# (sha256:4fcd39b758b660c4e9c345c021e2ea8f0ccdb31e3c32507d676cc3005ae83fba on Docker Hub on
# 2026-11-11), the most recent ROCm AMD supports on the Framework's gfx1151. VLLM_ROCM_FALLBACK
# names the build to fall back to if it fails to start or serve there: the release's ROCm 7.2
# build, v0.33.0-rocm72 (sha256:4fe7bc121cbe2f0791ebc38dcc2f0d615612233b4bfc0c1f4b9daeab05aba182),
# which a VLLM_ROCM_BUILD in the environment chooses for one run, with no edit here
# (VLLM_ROCM_BUILD=rocm72 host/engines vllm install). The audio image follows the same choice
# (host/vllm-rocm-audio/Dockerfile). Both digests are recorded there, where the build pins them.
#
# A row is a model and its server flags, in the rows file VLLM_ROWS names, beside this one.
# VLLM_MODEL_CUDA and VLLM_MODEL_ROCM name each flavor's default row; a VLLM_MODEL in the
# environment names another for one run, with no edit here (docs/engines/vllm/models.md,
# "Changing the model").
#
# On v0.33.0, a tag whose images (vllm/vllm-openai:v0.33.0, arm64 among them, and
# vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:v0.33.0) are built from the same commit as v0.33.0rc3, 4ba787ec99. GitHub's
# release object for that commit is still named v0.33.0rc3, so currency reports the pin against
# v0.33.0rc3 until the release moves. vLLM returns to the hosts for spike-model-layout's agent-vllm
# task (docs/findings/agent-vllm.md there), which serves gpt-oss-120b's agent rows on it.
VLLM_RELEASE=v0.33.0
VLLM_REPOSITORY_CUDA=vllm/vllm-openai
VLLM_REPOSITORY_ROCM=vllm/vllm-openai-rocm
VLLM_ROWS=vllm-rows
VLLM_MODEL_CUDA=gemma-4-26B-A4B-NVFP4
VLLM_MODEL_ROCM=gpt-oss-120b
VLLM_ROCM_FALLBACK=rocm72

# Native vLLM's Python (vllm-native.sh): the CPython minor version uv installs for each release's
# virtualenv. Held on 3.12, the image's Python, so the two hosting methods differ only in how they
# are hosted, and currency reports Python behind its latest until it moves. Native vLLM is retired
# on both hosts, so nothing moves it now: it stays held until vLLM's pins are removed.
VLLM_NATIVE_PYTHON=3.12
